// The toast stack. Rows are created into this from BattleRoyaleToasts.BuildRows() and positioned
// with SetPos, so this file declares no children of its own.
//
// The full-screen `size 1 1` + `hexactsize 0` frame is the ONE container shape whose GetScreenSize()
// reports real pixels, which is what makes a script SetPos in real pixels land where it was asked to.
// map_markers_3d.layout and the party name tags rely on the same thing. Do not wrap the rows in an
// intermediate sized panel: a declared position/size is scaled by viewport/1920 while SetPos is not,
// and mixing the two shifts the whole group while its internal spacing stays perfect - which reads
// as anything but a coordinate bug.
//
// priority sits above the world markers (40) and the two floating tag overlays (50), and below the
// death screen (900) - a dead player is being asked a question and a toast must not cover it.
FrameWidgetClass BattleRoyaleToastsRoot {
 visible 1
 ignorepointer 1
 clipchildren 0
 color 1 1 1 1
 position 0 0
 size 1 1
 hexactpos 0
 vexactpos 0
 hexactsize 0
 vexactsize 0
 priority 60
}
